{"hits": {"hits": [{"metadata": {"authors": [{"full_name": "Catani, S."}, {"full_name": "Trentadue, L."}], "publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "327", "page_end": "352", "year": 1989, "page_start": "323", "journal_title": "Nucl.Phys.B"}], "texkeys": ["Catani:1989ne"], "imprints": [{"date": "1989"}], "abstracts": [{"value": "We study the region of inhibited radiation in hard hadronic processes, as for jet cross sections and heavy flavour production near threshold. The cases of deep inelastic scattering and Drell-Yan annihilation are explicitly considered. A general method to exponentiate leading and next-to-leading logarithms to all orders in perturbation theory is developed. A complete formula for the large N -moments is given and shown to agree with previous two-loop calculations. The resummation procedure suggests how to connect the perturbative and nonperturbative regions. The natural limit within the perturbative phase is shown to be the intrinsic transverse momentum."}], "control_number": 25461, "dois": [{"value": "10.1016/0550-3213(89)90273-3"}], "titles": [{"title": "Resummation of the QCD Perturbative Series for Hard Processes"}, {"title": "QUANTUM CHROMODYNAMICS"}], "author_count": 2, "document_type": ["article"]}, "created": "1989-04-10T00:00:00+00:00", "updated": "2023-03-07T01:41:19.140377+00:00", "links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/25461?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/25461?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/25461?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/25461?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/25461?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/25461?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A25461"}, "id": "25461"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?sort=mostcited&q=j%20Nucl.Phys.B%2C327%2C323&size